{
  "name": "GenViData: SARS-CoV-2 Nanopore reads to lineage, variants and an Irish-Swedish comparison",
  "a_galaxy_workflow": "true",
  "format-version": "0.1",
  "annotation": "Runs one Irish sample of concern and Swedish samples through the same steps.\nThe Irish and Swedish reads come from different primer schemes, so each has its own branch\n(same subworkflows, different primer file and read length filter).\n1. Variation: the IWC workflow \"COVID-19: variation analysis of ARTIC ONT data\" (BY-COVID collection)\n   fastp, minimap2, ivar trim, medaka, lofreq filter, SnpEff -> annotated variants (VCF), QC reports\n2. Consensus: the IWC workflow \"COVID-19: consensus construction\" -> one consensus sequence per sample\n3. Join the Irish, Swedish and Swedish ENA consensus sequences in one FASTA file\n4. Lineage and mutations: Nextclade\n5. Distances: snp-dists on the Nextclade alignment\n6. Variant tables: SnpSift Extract Fields on the annotated variants\nReads are fetched by Galaxy from ENA, using the URLs in the job file made by scripts/02_make_job.py.\n",
  "tags": [],
  "uuid": "123c6308-eb09-49bb-82de-23aa8ae54612",
  "creator": [
    {
      "name": "ELIXIR Ireland",
      "class": "Organization"
    }
  ],
  "comments": [],
